# Bug TrackingPurpose:  Central bug tracking for the SDDRA system. Bugs are tracked  as decisions with specific workflow.Bug States:  REPORTED: Bug reported by user or detected by system  CONFIRMED: Bug confirmed by human  IN_PROGRESS: Fix in progress  RESOLVED: Fix implemented  VERIFIED: Fix verified by tests  CLOSED: Bug closedBug Priority:  CRITICAL: System unusable, data loss  HIGH: Major feature broken, workaround available  MEDIUM: Minor feature broken, workaround available  LOW: Cosmetic issue, no workaround neededBug Template:  ID: BUG-XXX  Title: <short description>  Priority: <CRITICAL|HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW>  Status: <state>  Reported_By: <user|system>  Reported_At: <timestamp>  Component: <.sdd/ component>  Description: <detailed description>  Steps_To_Reproduce:    - <step 1>    - <step 2>  Expected_Behavior: <what should happen>  Actual_Behavior: <what actually happens>  Workaround: <if any>  Fix_Approach: <how to fix>  Related_Decisions: [<DEC-IDs>]  Resolved_At: <timestamp>  Resolved_By: <who>  Verification: <how verified>Known Issues:  None currentlyRecent Bugs:  See decisions/ for bug-related decisionsState: +

Owns: projects\{project_name}\bugs\INDEX.sdd

State: +
